.TH "YAMLR-STATS" "1" "May 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
.SH "NAME"
yamlr-stats \- Propose repairs and remediate Kubernetes manifests.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
[PRO] Display surgical ROI, engineering time saved, and project safety metrics.
.PP
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
.RS
yamlr stats
yamlr stats --apps
.RE
.fi
.SH "FLAGS"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB--apps\fR: Group safety scores and top risks by application (inferred from labels or directory structure).
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB--badge\fR: Generate a shareable Markdown ROI badge (Shields.io) for your repository README.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB--org\fR: Show organization-wide surgical impact across all projects on this machine.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB--output\fR: Output format (\fBtext\fR or \fBjson\fR).
.SS " Universal Expert Flags"
Available across primary commands:
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB\fB--timing\fR\fR: [PERFORMANCE] Output surgical execution timing breakdown.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB\fB--timing-file <FILE>\fR\fR: [PERFORMANCE] Save performance profiling data to a JSON file.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB\fB--verbose\fR\fR: Full audit logs and engine stages.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB-q\fR, \fB--quiet\fR: Minimal output mode (exit codes only).
.SH "REPORTING BUGS"
Report bugs to <https://github.com/yamlr/yamlr/issues>
.PP
